    <Prose>
      <h1>Hermione Google connection privacy policy</h1>
      <p>Effective 28 October 2026. This policy covers the private Google Workspace connection used by Hermione, Dan Starr’s AI assistant running on Hermes Agent. It does not replace privacy notices for DannStarr Electronics repair services, RepairKeeper, Google or other independently operated services.</p>
      <h2>Who operates the connection</h2>
      <p>Dan Starr, trading as DannStarr Electronics, United Kingdom, controls this connection and its use of authorised account data. Contact: <a href="mailto:dannstarrelectronics@gmail.com">dannstarrelectronics@gmail.com</a>. The connection is for the operator’s authorised accounts, not an open service for connecting the public’s Google accounts.</p>
      <h2>Google data accessed</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Gmail:</strong> message headers, recipients, conversation identifiers, bodies, labels, drafts and attachments when relevant to an authorised task. Granted permissions also allow sending messages and modifying mailbox content; these capabilities remain subject to the operator’s instructions.</li>
        <li><strong>Calendar:</strong> calendar and event information, including participants, times and descriptions; creating or changing events when authorised.</li>
        <li><strong>Drive, Docs and Sheets:</strong> file metadata, document and spreadsheet contents, and file operations such as creation, editing, sharing or deletion when authorised.</li>
        <li><strong>Contacts:</strong> contact details through read-only access. This connection does not request contact-editing permission.</li>
        <li><strong>Authorisation data:</strong> OAuth credentials and tokens needed to maintain the account connection.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Permissions describe technical capability, not a commitment to copy the entire account or continuously monitor it. Relevant data is retrieved for requested work. Any routine monitoring or unattended actions require a separate operating policy.</p>
      <h2>Purposes and human oversight</h2>
      <p>Data is used to assist the operator with correspondence, draft preparation, customer-enquiry context, scheduling, document work and business administration. Gmail drafts are not sent merely because they exist. Formal repair approval, financial decisions and other commitments must not be inferred from free-text messages.</p>
      <p>Requested account assistance is based on the owner’s authorisation. Processing correspondence involving other people must also have an appropriate lawful basis for the relevant business purpose; OAuth permission from the account owner does not substitute for those obligations.</p>
      <h2>External processing and disclosure</h2>
      <p>Relevant task context may be transmitted to the configured AI model/API provider. The current assistant uses OpenAI through its Codex connection. AI responses and tool results may be retained in the assistant’s private session records. Data is therefore not guaranteed to remain entirely on the operator’s server. Provider processing and possible international transfers are subject to the provider’s applicable terms and safeguards.</p>
      <p>Google processes API requests. Other services receive relevant information only where needed for an authorised task, for example an email recipient, a calendar invitee or an explicitly authorised business-system integration. Private customer details must not be placed in public website pages or shared chat channels. Any chat-based review of customer-specific drafts must use an approved private destination.</p>
      <p>Google user data is not sold, used for advertising, or used by this application to build or train generalised AI or machine-learning models. It is not transferred to third parties for unrelated purposes. Access by the operator, or disclosure for security or legal obligations, is limited to what is necessary and permitted.</p>
      <h2>Storage and security</h2>
      <p>OAuth credentials are stored in restricted-access files on the operator-managed assistant host, separately from this public website and source repository. Google passwords are not collected by the assistant. Task context, conversation records and necessary operational references may be stored in private assistant storage; credentials or raw customer documents must not be copied into public repositories or general-purpose shared notes.</p>
      <p>Access restrictions, private network access and encrypted transport are used where applicable. No claim is made that every local record is encrypted at rest or that any system can guarantee absolute security.</p>
      <h2>Retention, deletion and your choices</h2>
      <p>Google originals remain subject to the account owner’s Gmail, Calendar and Drive settings. Local task records are retained as needed for requested work, continuity, troubleshooting and applicable business or legal recordkeeping, and should be reviewed and removed when no longer necessary. This connection does not promise automatic deletion after a fixed interval.</p>
      <p>The account owner can stop assistant use and revoke the connection through <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">Google Account connections</a>. Revocation stops future access through the revoked authorisation; it does not automatically erase previously retained records, messages already sent, or copies held by recipients or processing providers.</p>
      <p>Contact the operator to request access, correction, deletion or an explanation of retained personal information. Requests are subject to identity checks, applicable law, necessary retention obligations and the capabilities of relevant providers. UK data-protection concerns may also be raised with the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/">Information Commissioner’s Office</a>.</p>
      <h2>Google API Limited Use</h2>
      <p>Hermione’s use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.</p>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>This page will be updated when the connection’s data practices materially change, including changes to processing providers or unattended workflows. New or expanded permissions require appropriate authorisation.</p>
